# Result R10249

Task asked: Write a one-paragraph report comparing how fast CO2 at Mauna Loa rose in the last 5 complete years against the 5 years before, using NOAA GML annual means you download during the work. Give both ppm/yr averages and the ratio, with years, units and source URL.

Good result: Rates computed correctly from downloaded annual means; years/units right; source cited; one paragraph; nothing fabricated.

## Result

Using the NOAA GML Mauna Loa annual means (https://gml.noaa.gov/webdata/ccgg/trends/co2/co2_annmean_mlo.csv, fetched 2026-10-25 08:00:35 UTC, SHA-256 bdd956e8d7e05ebc3c61ac1f8f8c8cea4a505df56724fba5200b4eb1e0089b2b, kept unmodified as `data/co2_annmean_mlo.csv`), atmospheric CO2 rose by an average of 2.63 ppm per year over the last five complete years (2021–2025: (427.35 − 414.21)/5 = 2.628 ppm/yr, annual means in ppm) against 2.64 ppm per year over the five years before (2016–2020: (414.21 − 401.01)/5 = 2.640 ppm/yr), a ratio of 0.995 (2.628/2.640). The two periods thus show essentially the same average growth rate; each rate is the change in annual mean across the window, i.e. the mean of the five year-to-year increments, with 2020 and 2015 as base years.
